<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    THE ROLL, AND NOTHING ELSE. This assembly decides what an asset IS and never draws one, so it
    carries no imaging library and no package reference of any kind. That is the point of it: a host
    that only needs to roll — a game server, an engine, a tool — takes this and nothing else.

    It is also the ONLY definition of every decision an asset is made of. Nfty.Core's Generator calls
    into here rather than keeping a second copy of the roll, because two copies is how "the server
    and the client agree" stops being true.

    NO #if IN LOGIC. Should a second target framework ever be added, whatever it needs is written
    unconditionally: one code path cannot diverge from itself.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
